==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|chequer||UK}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtʃɛkə/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-checker.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈt͡ʃɛkɚ/|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛkə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|:af|check<id:verb>|-er<id:agent noun>|text=+|tree=1}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# One who or that which [[check]]s or verifies something.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Neil J. Salkind|title=Applying Macintosh: Solutions, Ideas, and Tools|publisher=[[w:Macmillan Inc.|Macmillan Publishing Company]]|year=1992|page=205|isbn=0-675-22133-1|passage=So, keep in mind that {{w|Microsoft Word}}’s Spelling tool is as much a “typo” tool as a '''checker''' of spelling.}}
# One who makes a check mark.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1989|author=M. Manfred Fabritius; William Borges|title=Saving the Savings and Loan
|passage="Essentially," said a senior vice president of the FHLBB of Dallas, "we were '''checkers''' of boxes."}}
# The [[clerk]] who tallies cost of purchases and accepts payment.
#: {{ux|en|There was a long line at the grocery store because the '''checker''' was so slow.}}
#* {{RQ:King Mist|passage=Bud Brown said something to the '''checker''' he was supervising; she had been craning around to see what was happening. She flushed and began to run her calculator again.}}
# One who hinders or stops something.

